   320→    requirements:
   321→      - _ulid: 01KF1XWKF10000000000000000
   322→        slugs:
   323→          - workflow-schema
   324→        title: Workflow Schema
   325→        type: requirement
   326→        status:
   327→          maturity: draft
   328→          implementation: not_started
   329→        description: |
   330→          Workflow definition structure:
   331→
   332→          ```yaml
   333→          - _ulid: 01KF...
   334→            id: spec-first         # Short identifier
   335→            trigger: behavior change
   336→            description: |
   337→              Check spec coverage before implementing changes.
   338→            steps:
   339→              - type: check
   340→                content: Does the spec cover this change?
   341→                on_fail: Update spec first
   342→              - type: action
   343→                content: Update spec if needed
   344→              - type: action
   345→                content: Derive task from spec
   346→              - type: action
   347→                content: Implement the change
   348→          ```
   349→
   350→          Steps have types: check, action, decision
   351→          on_fail provides guidance when checks fail.
   352→        implements:
   353→          - '@workflow-definitions'
   354→      - _ulid: 01KF1XWKF20000000000000000
   355→        slugs:
   356→          - workflow-steps
   357→        title: Workflow Step Types
   358→        type: requirement
   359→        status:
   360→          maturity: draft
   361→          implementation: not_started
   362→        description: |
   363→          Step types:
   364→
   365→          - check: Verification step (pass/fail)
   366→            Has on_fail for what to do if check fails
   367→
   368→          - action: Something to do
   369→            No conditional, just execute
   370→
   371→          - decision: Branch point
   372→            Has options for different paths
   373→
   374→          Steps are executed in order. Agents interpret them,
   375→          they're not automatically enforced.
   376→        implements:
   377→          - '@workflow-definitions'
   378→      - _ulid: 01KF2XWKF40000000000000000
   379→        slugs:
   380→          - workflow-execution-model
   381→        title: Workflow Execution Model
   382→        type: requirement
   383→        status:
   384→          maturity: draft
   385→          implementation: not_started
   386→        description: |
   387→          Workflows are ADVISORY, not AUTOMATED. This is a deliberate design choice.
   388→
   389→          Execution model options:
   390→
   391→          1. **Documentation** (default): Workflows exist as reference documentation.
   392→             Agents read them when relevant, but no runtime enforcement.
   393→             `kspec meta workflows` displays them for human/agent reference.
   394→
   395→          2. **Checklist**: Workflows can be displayed as interactive checklists.
   396→             `kspec meta run @workflow` presents steps one at a time,
   397→             agent confirms each step completion. Progress tracked but not enforced.
   398→
   399→          3. **Hook integration**: Workflows can inform Claude Code hooks.
   400→             A hook could query `kspec meta workflows --trigger "commit"`
   401→             and inject relevant workflow steps into the prompt.
   402→             Still advisory - hook provides context, agent decides.
   403→
   404→          Why not automation?
   405→          - Workflows describe nuanced processes that require judgment
   406→          - "Check if spec covers this" can't be reliably automated
   407→          - Automation creates brittleness; advisory enables adaptation
   408→          - Trust agents to follow documented processes
   409→
   410→          Future: Workflow adherence tracking via observations.
   411→          Friction observations on workflows indicate where guidance fails.
   412→          This creates a feedback loop: observe friction → improve workflow.
   413→
   414→          ```yaml
   415→          # Optional execution hints
   416→          steps:
   417→            - type: check
   418→              content: Does the spec cover this change?
   419→              on_fail: Update spec first
   420→              execution:
   421→                mode: prompt  # prompt, silent, or skip
   422→                timeout: null # Optional timeout for automated checks
   423→          ```
   424→
   425→          execution.mode values:
   426→          - prompt (default): Show step, wait for confirmation
   427→          - silent: Log step, don't wait
   428→          - skip: Skip in checklist mode (documentation only)
   429→        implements:
   430→          - '@workflow-definitions'
   431→      - _ulid: 01KF1XWKF30000000000000000
