   527→      - _ulid: 01KF1XCNV20000000000000000
   528→        slugs:
   529→          - convention-domains
   530→        title: Convention Domains
   531→        type: requirement
   532→        status:
   533→          maturity: draft
   534→          implementation: not_started
   535→        description: |
   536→          Standard convention domains:
   537→
   538→          - commits: Git commit message format
   539→          - notes: Task note writing style
   540→          - naming: Slug/identifier conventions
   541→          - tags: Tag taxonomy and usage
   542→          - branching: Git branch naming
   543→          - documentation: Doc writing standards
   544→
   545→          Projects can define custom domains as needed.
   546→        implements:
   547→          - '@convention-definitions'
   548→      - _ulid: 01KF2XCNV30000000000000000
   549→        slugs:
   550→          - convention-validation
   551→        title: Convention Validation Strategy
   552→        type: requirement
   553→        status:
   554→          maturity: draft
   555→          implementation: not_started
   556→        description: |
   557→          Conventions support optional validation with domain-specific strategies:
   558→
   559→          ```yaml
   560→          - _ulid: 01KF...
   561→            domain: commits
   562→            rules:
   563→              - Use conventional commit format
   564→            validation:
   565→              type: regex
   566→              pattern: "^(feat|fix|docs|style|refactor|test|chore)(\\(.+\\))?:\\s.+"
   567→              message: "Commit must follow conventional format"
   568→          ```
   569→
   570→          Validation types by domain:
   571→
   572→          - commits: regex pattern matching on message
   573→          - notes: word count range, required sections
   574→          - naming: regex pattern for slugs/identifiers
   575→          - tags: enum list of allowed tags
   576→          - branching: regex pattern for branch names
   577→          - documentation: prose (advisory only, no automation)
   578→
   579→          Validation configuration:
   580→
   581→          ```yaml
   582→          validation:
   583→            type: regex | enum | range | prose
   584→            # For regex:
   585→            pattern: "^pattern$"
   586→            message: "Error message when validation fails"
   587→            # For enum:
   588→            allowed: [value1, value2, value3]
   589→            # For range:
   590→            min: 10
   591→            max: 500
   592→            unit: words | chars | lines
   593→          ```
   594→
   595→          Validation is optional - conventions without validation field
   596→          are advisory-only and appear in documentation.
   597→
   598→          `kspec validate --conventions` runs all validatable conventions.
   599→          Prose-type conventions are skipped with info message.
   600→        implements:
   601→          - '@convention-definitions'
   602→  - _ulid: 01KF1XFBK00000000000000000
   603→    slugs:
   604→      - observations
   605→      - feedback-loop
   606→    title: Observations
   607→    type: feature
   608→    status:
   609→      maturity: draft
   610→      implementation: implemented
   611→    priority: high
   612→    tags:
   613→      - mvp
   614→      - meta
   615→      - feedback
   616→    description: |
   617→      Observations capture feedback about workflows and conventions.
   618→      This is the mechanism for the self-improvement loop - agents
   619→      record friction, success, questions, and ideas, then patterns
   620→      emerge that inform workflow improvements.
   621→
   622→      Observations can be promoted to tasks with --meta-ref, creating
   623→      trackable work to improve processes.
   624→    acceptance_criteria:
   625→      - id: ac-obs-1
   626→        given: an agent encounters workflow friction
   627→        when: kspec meta observe friction "description" runs
   628→        then: >
   629→          outputs "OK Created observation: <ULID-prefix>"; observation stored with fields: _ulid,
   630→          type, content, created_at (ISO8601), author, resolved (false), workflow_ref (if --workflow
   631→          provided)
   632→      - id: ac-obs-2
   633→        given: observations exist
   634→        when: kspec meta observations runs
   635→        then: >
   636→          outputs table with columns: ID, Type, Workflow, Created, Content (truncated); shows only
   637→          unresolved by default; --all includes resolved
   638→      - id: ac-obs-3
   639→        given: an observation exists
   640→        when: kspec meta promote @obs --title "Task title" runs
   641→        then: >
   642→          creates task with: title from --title, description from observation content, meta_ref from
   643→          observation's workflow_ref; outputs "OK Created task: <ULID-prefix>"; observation updated
   644→          with promoted_to field pointing to new task
   645→      - id: ac-obs-4
   646→        given: an observation exists
   647→        when: kspec meta resolve @obs "resolution text" runs
   648→        then: >
   649→          observation updated with: resolved=true, resolution=text, resolved_at (ISO8601),
   650→          resolved_by (author); outputs "OK Resolved: <ULID-prefix>"
   651→      - id: ac-obs-5
   652→        given: kspec meta observations --json runs
   653→        when: observations exist
   654→        then: |
   655→          outputs JSON array with full observation objects including all fields
   656→      - id: ac-obs-6
   657→        given: an observation has already been promoted (has promoted_to field)
   658→        when: kspec meta promote @obs runs
   659→        then: >
   660→          exits with code 1; error message: "Observation already promoted to task <task-ref>;
   661→          resolve or delete the task first"
   662→      - id: ac-obs-7
   663→        given: an observation is already resolved (resolved=true)
   664→        when: kspec meta resolve @obs runs
   665→        then: >
   666→          exits with code 1; error message: "Observation already resolved on <date>:
   667→          '<resolution-text-truncated>'"
   668→      - id: ac-obs-8
   669→        given: an observation is already resolved
   670→        when: kspec meta promote @obs runs
   671→        then: >
   672→          exits with code 1; error message: "Cannot promote resolved observation; use --force to
   673→          override"
   674→      - id: ac-obs-9
   675→        given: an observation has promoted_to pointing to a completed task
   676→        when: kspec meta resolve @obs runs with no explicit resolution
   677→        then: >
   678→          auto-populates resolution from task completion reason if available; prompts for resolution
   679→          text if task has no completion reason
