   682→        slugs:
   683→          - observation-schema
   684→        title: Observation Schema
   685→        type: requirement
   686→        status:
   687→          maturity: draft
   688→          implementation: not_started
   689→        description: |
   690→          Observation structure:
   691→
   692→          ```yaml
   693→          - _ulid: 01KF...
   694→            type: friction        # friction, success, question, idea
   695→            workflow_ref: "@spec-first"  # Related workflow (optional)
   696→            content: |
   697→              Spec-first check feels heavyweight for typo fixes.
   698→              Interrupts flow for trivial changes.
   699→            created_at: "2025-01-15T10:00:00Z"
   700→            author: "@claude"
   701→            resolved: false
   702→            resolution: null      # Filled when resolved
   703→          ```
   704→
   705→          Types capture the nature of the feedback.
   706→          workflow_ref links to relevant workflow for tracking.
   707→        implements:
   708→          - '@observations'
   709→      - _ulid: 01KF1XFBK20000000000000000
   710→        slugs:
   711→          - observation-types
   712→        title: Observation Types
   713→        type: requirement
   714→        status:
   715→          maturity: draft
   716→          implementation: not_started
   717→        description: |
   718→          Observation types:
   719→
   720→          - friction: Something that's hard, slow, or frustrating
   721→          - success: Something that works well (positive feedback)
   722→          - question: Uncertainty about how to proceed
   723→          - idea: Potential improvement or new approach
   724→
   725→          All types feed the improvement loop. Friction and ideas
   726→          most often lead to workflow changes. Success confirms
   727→          what's working. Questions may reveal documentation gaps.
   728→        implements:
   729→          - '@observations'
   730→      - _ulid: 01KF1XFBK30000000000000000
   731→        slugs:
   732→          - observation-promotion
   733→        title: Observation Promotion
   734→        type: requirement
   735→        status:
   736→          maturity: draft
   737→          implementation: not_started
   738→        description: |
   739→          Observations can be promoted to tasks:
   740→
   741→          ```bash
   742→          kspec meta promote @obs-123 \
   743→            --title "Simplify spec-first for trivial changes" \
   744→            --priority 2
   745→          ```
   746→
   747→          Creates task with:
   748→          - title from --title
   749→          - meta_ref pointing to related workflow
   750→          - description from observation content
   751→          - origin: observation_promotion
   752→
   753→          Original observation marked with promoted_to reference.
   754→        implements:
   755→          - '@observations'
   756→      - _ulid: 01KF1XFBK40000000000000000
   757→        slugs:
   758→          - observation-resolution
   759→        title: Observation Resolution
   760→        type: requirement
   761→        status:
   762→          maturity: draft
   763→          implementation: not_started
   764→        description: |
   765→          Resolving observations:
   766→
   767→          ```bash
   768→          kspec meta resolve @obs-123 "Addressed by --quick flag in v0.2"
   769→          ```
   770→
   771→          Sets:
   772→          - resolved: true
   773→          - resolution: "Addressed by --quick flag in v0.2"
   774→          - resolved_at: timestamp
   775→          - resolved_by: author
   776→
   777→          Resolved observations remain for history.
   778→          Unresolved observations show in session context.
   779→        implements:
   780→          - '@observations'
   781→      - _ulid: 01KF2XFBK50000000000000000
   782→        slugs:
   783→          - observation-task-loop
   784→        title: Observation-Task Resolution Loop
   785→        type: requirement
   786→        status:
   787→          maturity: draft
   788→          implementation: not_started
   789→        description: |
   790→          The observation→task→resolution loop defines how observations connect
   791→          to tasks and when they get resolved.
   792→
   793→          **Promotion creates linkage**:
   794→          When an observation is promoted to a task:
   795→          - observation.promoted_to = @task-ref
   796→          - task.origin = "observation_promotion"
   797→          - task.description includes observation content
   798→
   799→          **Task completion does NOT auto-resolve**:
   800→          Completing a task does not automatically resolve linked observations.
   801→          This is intentional:
   802→          - Task might address the observation partially
   803→          - Multiple tasks might be needed
   804→          - Agent should explicitly confirm resolution
   805→
   806→          **Explicit resolution required**:
   807→          After completing the task, agent runs:
   808→          ```bash
   809→          kspec meta resolve @obs "Addressed by task @task-ref"
   810→          ```
   811→
   812→          **Convenience: resolve-from-task**:
   813→          If observation has promoted_to pointing to a completed task:
   814→          ```bash
   815→          kspec meta resolve @obs
   816→          # Auto-populates: "Resolved via task @task-ref: <task.reason>"
   817→          ```
   818→          Prompts for resolution text if task has no completion reason.
   819→
   820→          **Session context reminder**:
   821→          When task with origin="observation_promotion" is completed,
   822→          session context shows reminder:
   823→          "Consider resolving linked observation: @obs-ref"
   824→
   825→          **Querying the loop**:
   826→          ```bash
   827→          # Find observations that spawned tasks
   828→          kspec meta observations --promoted
   829→
   830→          # Find tasks from observations
   831→          kspec tasks list --origin observation_promotion
   832→
   833→          # Find unresolved observations with completed tasks
   834→          kspec meta observations --pending-resolution
   835→          ```
   836→
   837→          This explicit loop ensures observations aren't lost when tasks
   838→          complete, and creates traceable process improvement history.
   839→        implements:
   840→          - '@observations'
